                "region": {
                  "endLine": 105,
                  "startLine": 103
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Captured payments are acknowledged even when recording them fails\n\nA captured-payment notification can receive `200` while its database write failed and the account remains unpaid. When the browser callback is unavailable, the application has acknowledged its recovery event without recording the payment.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Payment processing reliability financial integrity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-703\n\nRemediation:\nAcknowledge only after durably storing the event or applying the payment update. Return a retryable failure for transient storage errors; implement an idempotent durable inbox/reconciliation worker and alert on irreconcilable events. Verify gateway state server-side before offering another payment.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Force one storage failure during capture; require retryable response or durable queued event.\n- Replay the same capture after recovery and assert one paid transition and no duplicate charge.\n- Lose the browser callback and verify eventual paid-state recovery."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:fc1b0e47bf87f82366bf06e4bf81846f4ebb875ac3524550f637c1841fe8f311",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "d15582a43b8ce4b1:1"
          },
          "properties": {
