          "message": {
            "text": "Clinical write failures send clinical fields to server logs\n\nFailed clinical-work inserts and edits print complete database error objects to `console.error`. Those query errors can contain bound patient case identifiers and clinical findings, copying clinical data into operational log systems.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Sensitive clinical information in logs\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-532\n\nRemediation:\nRemove the two raw console calls. Log only operation, vetted IDs/status and safe error codes. Check local catches elsewhere for equivalent raw-error logging. Test failure paths with synthetic sensitive markers and assert none reach console/logger output.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Induce insert and update failures with synthetic clinical markers; assert no marker appears in console or logger calls.\n- Check that client responses remain generic and ownership guards still apply."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:425bb61b8c6264108a63f859838bb7b416edfada4b50dba585fee30b2623244a",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "4abdf4777936a282:1"
          },
          "properties": {
