                "region": {
                  "endLine": 88,
                  "startLine": 84
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Deleting an applicant also removes outstanding payment linkage\n\nHard-deleting a pending applicant removes every payment row, including an outstanding checkout order. A later genuine capture then has no account mapping and is acknowledged without recording it. Deleting a paid account also removes local payment/refund reference data.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Payment ledger retention reconciliation reliability\n\nRemediation:\nDefine payment retention independently of account deletion. Keep a financial tombstone/provider identifiers and block or reconcile outstanding payments before removal. Avoid recreating clinical/personal records merely to retain a receipt.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- An account with an unsettled order must not lose its reconciliation mapping.\n- A later capture after permitted account deletion must be durably correlated for refund/reconciliation."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:1ff80aaf09162dc7d90de5d1a13ed6cde772684a14a1b5cc356d107c481f5e4b",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "17c6923bf7dd6cec:1"
          },
